  "nonclaims": [
    "Lifecycle purpose is governed metadata; module and composition guests still must prove that command semantics and effects satisfy it.",
    "V1 rejects a command that consumes objects from two creating releases in the same lane; same-lane cross-release coordination remains unimplemented.",
    "The resolver does not prove conservation, custody, liabilities, reserves, fee allocation, replay consumption, terminal obligations, migration continuity, or outbox semantics.",
    "No Python/Tau/Lean/Kani refinement, RISC0 guest, release-aware epoch verifier, current-head check, ZenoLedger commit, API/UI mount, or value-moving path is added.",
    "No RC, production-readiness, formal-verification, whole-economy proof, or whole-economy settlement claim is promoted."
  ]
